{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>You shall not eat it, etc., for you shall do what is right in the eyes of HaShem.</b> And when you refrain from eating it, this is not as one who finds it repulsive, but rather so that you may do what is right in the eyes of HaShem. As they said, of blessed memory (Torat Kohanim Kedoshim 9:10): אַל יֹאמַר אִי אֶפְשִׁי בִּבְשַׂר חֲזִיר, אֲבָל יֹאמַר אֶפְשִׁי וְאֶפְשִׁי וְאָבִי שֶׁבַּשָּׁמַיִם גָּזַר עָלַי (Let him not say 'it is impossible regarding the flesh of a pig,' but rather let him say 'it is possible, it is possible, but my Father in heaven has decreed it upon me')."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:21:20.015519762Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}